Server hardening: `helmet`, CORS allowlist from `CLIENT_ORIGIN` (comma-separated), `compression`, `trust proxy` = 1 (Render), JSON body limit 100kb, request IDs, structured `pino` logs without PII, graceful shutdown on SIGTERM (drain HTTP, close queues), global error handler, per-IP and per-user rate limits backed by Redis.

# 17. SCALABILITY AND RELIABILITY ("any number of users" means scale by configuration, not rewrites)

- Stateless API and worker, scale each independently by instance count (Render) with no code changes. Redis (Render Key Value) holds queues and limiter state.
- Firestore auto-scales. Avoid hot documents (no global counters on a single doc; usage docs are per user per month). Cache the recipe library and price books in-process with TTL and version invalidation.
- Backpressure: a queue-depth cap returns `429` with `Retry-After` and a friendly "We're busy, you're #n in line" state. Jobs are retried with backoff and moved to a dead-letter queue after N attempts.
- The recipe library amortizes AI cost across all users: the more people use it, the fewer AI calls per plan.
- Client performance: route-level code splitting, TanStack Query caching, Firestore listeners scoped to the open plan only, image `srcSet` plus lazy loading, long-lived immutable asset caching, Lighthouse targets of 90+ on performance, accessibility, best practices and SEO on the landing page.
- Document the real limits in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`: Gemini quota tier, Firestore limits, Render instance sizes, and how to raise each.

